# Provider API keys for the dsh agent (model access, and web_search).
# Copy to .env and fill in the ones you have. Do not commit .env.
#
# Every variable in this file is passed into the container (compose `env_file`),
# and dsh resolves it by name for the matching model provider. Leave a key out
# (or blank) and that provider is simply unavailable; nothing else breaks.
#
# DeepSeek's own API — used by the built-in `deepseek-official` route and by the
# web_search tool. Keep this set if you want DeepSeek models or web search.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# Vercel AI Gateway — one key for DeepSeek, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, and
# many more. Create one at https://vercel.com/ai-gateway
# Not required for the built-in deepseek-official route.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...
#
# Other pi-ai catalog providers. Uncomment the key you have, then either
# uncomment the matching route in global-agent-config/cordis.patch.yml or add
# the provider from the Web UI's Models page.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
# GROQ_API_KEY=...
# XAI_API_KEY=...
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=...
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=...
# ZAI_API_KEY=...
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=...
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=...
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=...
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=...
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=...
# HF_TOKEN=...
#
# Any other provider or self-hosted OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible endpoint: put
# its key here under the name you reference from the route's apiKeyEnv.
# MY_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...
